ASK 8 – Implement and Test the Algorithms
The following Python program implements all three algorithms selected in Task 1:
1. Linear Search – Iterative, Brute Force.
2. Recursive Binary Search – Divide and Conquer.
3. Hash Table Search – Hashing with separate chaining.
It tests the same registration-number datasets at 1,000, 10,000, 100,000 and 1,000,000 records. It records execution time and the number of key comparisons.

The program also:
- Checks whether all three algorithms return the correct result.
- Measures sorting and hash-table construction separately.
- Saves experimental results in a CSV file.
- Generates performance graphs.
