3. Test cases
Test case	Input condition	Expected result
TC01	Target is present	Registration number found
TC02	Target is absent	Registration number not found
TC03	Target is first element	Linear Search finds it immediately
TC04	Target is last element	Linear Search checks all elements
TC05	Target is in middle of sorted list	Binary Search finds it
TC06	Dataset contains 1,000 records	All algorithms return correct result
TC07	Dataset contains 1,000,000 records	All algorithms return correct result

The main experiment uses the last element of the shuffled dataset as the target. This gives Linear Search its worst-case condition. Binary Search and Hash Table Search use the same target and equivalent registration-number data.
